id: E340
trigger_tool: configure|make
phase: configuration|packaging
error_signature: The intltool scripts were not found.*Please install intltool|intltool-update.*not found|intltool-merge.*not found
severity: 3
category: ohos, autotools, intltool, desktop-entry, conan
match_keywords: OHOS, HarmonyOS, Autotools, intltool, intltool-update, intltool-merge, desktop-file, .desktop.in, configure
title: Keep legacy Autotools desktop metadata builds independent of unavailable intltool

root_cause: The release configure script unconditionally expands IT_PROG_INTLTOOL and fails when intltool-update, intltool-merge, or intltool-extract is absent. The data Makefile then uses intltool-merge to turn .desktop.in files into .desktop files. On OHOS, the runner commonly lacks intltool. Runtime confirmation for this package is Needs verification until W3 runs on the target worker.
affected_scope: Legacy Autotools desktop applications whose release tarball contains generated configure and Makefile.in files, but whose package only needs the standard desktop-entry keys and does not require translated metadata.
verification_cmd: Apply the recipe patches to a clean release tarball, run ./configure --disable-nls with the recipe-local probe tools on PATH, run make -j1, inspect data/*.desktop for Name/Exec/Type, then run make check on a worker with desktop-file-validate.

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: package-local-intltool-probe-and-desktop-rule
rec_description: Remove IT_PROG_INTLTOOL from configure.ac for future regeneration; keep the generated configure usable with build-folder-only probe shims that report the required version; replace the data Makefile desktop rule with a deterministic sed conversion for underscore-prefixed keys. Do not package the shims.
rec_command: conan create archives/a/activity-log-manager/0.9.7 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe-and-source-patch

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: real-intltool-build-requirement
fallback_description: If translated desktop metadata is required, provide a real published intltool-compatible build requirement and retain the upstream merge rule. The fallback is preferred over stripping translations.
fallback_command: conan create archives/a/activity-log-manager/0.9.7 --build=missing
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: dependency

forbid_1_pattern: disable.*all.*tests|skip.*make check|replace.*make check.*true
forbid_1_reason: The missing intltool utility must not be hidden by removing the upstream validation target.
forbid_1_consequence: The package can appear green without validating installed desktop metadata.
forbid_2_pattern: install.*intltool.*globally|patch.*ci/|modify.*runner.*PATH
forbid_2_reason: A single package must keep its build-tool workaround inside its own recipe.
forbid_2_consequence: The adaptation becomes non-reproducible and violates one-software PR atomicity.

principles: P013,P014
